        <body>
            <div xml:id="d771">

                <pb facs="1053" n="1043" sameAs="frus:frus1946v10/pg1043"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.241/7–246: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. William E.
                            Vogelback to Mr. Thomas B.
                            McCabe
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Manila</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-07-02">2 July 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3719. Pending the execution of firm contract with China, a policy has been
                    adopted to govern action of Pacific Field Commissioners, which recognizes
                    possible moral obligation to cease disposals earliest possible date on one hand
                    and the damaging effects which would inevitably follow the cessation of selling
                    operations on the other. Sales will continue except that large contracts
                    involving 1 million dollars <pb facs="1054" n="1044" xml:id="pg1044"/> or more
                    in realization will be discussed with China with intention of securing waivers.
                    Until July 15th sales will be unconditionally for account of US Government
                    coinciding in date with loading of ships now dockside. Beginning July 16th sales
                    will be earmarked as tentatively for China account but at no time to exceed the
                    last 30 days cumulative sales. This will be used as incentive to speedy
                    agreement and other purposes.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
